<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Resource-shrinker keep list (consumed by AGP when `shrinkResources true`).

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
  The Google Mobile Ads SDK (com.google.android.gms:play-services-ads) ships
  res/xml/gma_ad_services_config.xml and references it ONLY through a manifest property the
  SDK injects into the merged manifest:
      <property android:name="android.adservices.AD_SERVICES_CONFIG"
                android:resource="@xml/gma_ad_services_config" />
  AGP's resource shrinker does NOT treat a manifest <property android:resource=...> as a use of
  the resource, so it strips the resource-table entry for @xml/gma_ad_services_config while the
  file itself still ships inside the .aab. Google Play Console then rejects the upload:
      "Module 'base' contains resource files that are not referenced from the resource table:
       res/xml/gma_ad_services_config.xml"
  (bundletool build-apks validation). Keeping the entry here restores file/table consistency so
  every generated .aab uploads cleanly.

  If a mediation adapter later adds another *_ad_services_config.xml with the same
  manifest-property-only reference and triggers the same rejection, add it to tools:keep too.

  THE ADAPTIVE ICON PIECES are pinned for a related-but-different reason. @mipmap/ic_launcher_fg
  and @color/ic_launcher_bg are referenced ONLY from mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher{,_round}.xml,
  and the generated app's launcher icon is the one resource the shrinker cannot see being used —
  AppMint writes the manifest itself, so no source in this module points at it. If either got
  stripped, generated apps would fall back to the legacy bitmap and the white launcher frame this
  adaptive icon exists to remove would silently come back.

  THE ALTERNATE ICON SLOTS (ic_launcher_alt1..4, their _fg layers and _bg colours, 2026-09-30) are
  pinned for the same reason: only the generated manifest's launcher <activity-alias> entries point
  at them (AppIconSwitcher), and the generator fills them per build. Their ids are resolved by name
  (TemplateResourceIds.altIcons), so a stripped slot would fail the app build, not ship a dead icon.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@xml/gma_ad_services_config,@string/google_app_id,@xml/appwright_widget_info,@layout/appwright_widget,@layout/appwright_widget_preview,@layout/appwright_widget_rich,@drawable/appmint_tv_banner,@mipmap/ic_launcher,@mipmap/ic_launcher_round,@mipmap/ic_launcher_fg,@color/ic_launcher_bg,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt1,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt1_fg,@color/ic_launcher_alt1_bg,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt2,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt2_fg,@color/ic_launcher_alt2_bg,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt3,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt3_fg,@color/ic_launcher_alt3_bg,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt4,@mipmap/ic_launcher_alt4_fg,@color/ic_launcher_alt4_bg" />

